  "intro": "<p>Diabetic meal planning for restaurant visits is a structured approach that helps you choose foods and portions that keep blood sugar steady while enjoying dining out. By focusing on balanced macronutrients, fiber, and low‑glycemic options, you can reduce spikes and support long‑term metabolic health. This guide explains how to plan, track, and adapt your meals so you stay in control of your glucose levels, even when eating at restaurants.</p>\n",
